{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection","title":"def:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.md","line":311,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex#def:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-affine-connection]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex","label":"def:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection","line":647,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Riemannian connection]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0071,petersen:page-0073}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch2-affine-connection}\n\n  An affine connection in the sense of\n  \\cref{def:pet-ch2-affine-connection} on $(M,g)$\n  is \\emph{Riemannian} if it is torsion free and metric-compatible:\n  \\[\n    \\nabla_XY-\\nabla_YX=[X,Y],\n    \\qquad\n    D_Zg(X,Y)=g(\\nabla_ZX,Y)+g(X,\\nabla_ZY).\n  \\]\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Riemannian connection] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368322d7269656d616e6e69616e2d636f6e6e656374696f6e\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0071, petersen:page-0073</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-affine-connection\">↗ def:pet-ch2-affine-connection</a> <p></p>An affine connection in the sense of <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-affine-connection\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blu